ADD-RES    (COMP,THEO).The determination of astrophysical         A0007  2    5 
           factor was made. The correlation of total              A0007  2    6 
           cross sections of the T(t,2n)He-4 and He-3(He3,2p)He-4 A0007  2    7 
           reactions is discussed.                                A0007  2    8 
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-T).Accidental error of total cross-section        A0007  2    9 
            includes ERR-S and ERR-SYS.                           A0007  2   10 
           (ERR-S,1.,5.) It is conditioned by statistical errors  A0007  2   11 
            of measurement (1-5%),                                A0007  2   12 
           (ERR-SYS) In the values of total cross-sections        A0007  2   13 
           systematic error +-7% is possible. This error          A0007  2   14 
           is connected with accuracy of determining the          A0007  2   15 
           coefficient of anisotropy includes:                    A0007  2   16 
           (ERR-1) errors in determination gas pressure (+-3%) andA0007  2   17 
           (ERR-2) concentration of tritium  (+-5%).              A0007  2   18 
           (EN-ERR).Essential error of measurement-error of       A0007  2   19 
           determination the energy of tritons in exit of gas     A0007  2   20 
           target window.                                         A0007  2   21 
SAMPLE     Gas target 1-H-3 with thin entrance window of          A0007  2   22 
           aluminum  oxide, thickness 50 microgram/cm**2.         A0007  2   23 
           inside of target and in front of it Li-F-targets       A0007  2   24 
           for determination of energy loss of accelerated        A0007  2   25 
           particles in entrance window of gas target were        A0007  2   26 
           placed.                                                A0007  2   27 
ANALYSIS   (INTAD).Angular distributions of neutron yields were   A0007  2   28 
           measured for triton energies of 52 and 76 keV in the   A0007  2   29 
           angular interval from 0 degree to 150 degree. Later on A0007  2   30 
           interpolation for energy and repeated counting         A0007  2   31 
           from 0 degree to 180 degree were made.                 A0007  2   32 
